ling"}],[{"text":"GMP"},{"text":"Good Manufacturing Practices"}],[{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"BMR, BPR, SOPs, logbooks"}],[{"text":"Quality"},{"text":"In-process controls, specifications"}],[{"text":"Validation"},{"text":"Process, cleaning, equipment validation concepts"}],[{"text":"Production Planning"},{"text":"Scheduling and resource coordination"}],[{"text":"Equipment"},{"text":"Manufacturing equipment operation"}],[{"text":"Safety"},{"text":"Industrial and pharmaceutical safety"}],[{"text":"Data"},{"text":"Production records and trend analysis"}],[{"text":"Compliance"},{"text":"GMP and regulatory requirements"}],[{"text":"Problem Solving"},{"text":"Deviation and root-cause analysis"}]]}]},{"heading":"Pharmaceutical Manufacturing Workflow","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Production Plan"},{"type":"h","text":"Material Availability Check"},{"type":"h","text":"Dispensing"},{"type":"h","text":"Line Clearance"},{"type":"h","text":"Equipment Readiness"},{"type":"h","text":"Manufacturing Process"},{"type":"h","text":"In-Process Controls"},{"type":"h","text":"Yield / Reconciliation"},{"type":"h","text":"Packaging"},{"type":"h","text":"Final Documentation Review"},{"type":"h","text":"QA Review"},{"type":"h","text":"Batch Release"},{"type":"p","text":"A Production Executive does not independently release finished batches merely because manufacturing is complete; Quality Assurance has an independent quality role in batch disposition/release according to the site's quality system and applicable regulations."}]},{"heading":"GMP Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Good Manufacturing Practice is central to pharmaceutical production."},{"type":"h","text":"A student should understand:"},{"type":"h","text":"Documentation"},{"type":"h","text":"SOPs"},{"type":"h","text":"Batch Manufacturing Records"},{"type":"h","text":"Batch Packaging Records"},{"type":"h","text":"Equipment logbooks"},{"type":"h","text":"Cleaning records"},{"type":"h","text":"Training records"},{"type":"h","text":"Quality Systems"},{"type":"h","text":"Deviations"},{"type":"h","text":"CAPA"},{"type":"h","text":"Change control"},{"type":"h","text":"OOS/OOT concepts"},{"type":"h","text":"Risk assessment"},{"type":"h","text":"Audit readiness"},{"type":"h","text":"Data integrity"},{"type":"h","text":"Manufacturing Discipline"},{"type":"h","text":"Line clearance"},{"type":"h","text":"Status labelling"},{"type":"h","text":"Material traceability"},{"type":"h","text":"Cross-contamination prevention"},{"type":"h","text":"Cleaning procedures"},{"type":"h","text":"Personnel hygiene"},{"type":"h","text":"Environmental controls"}]},{"heading":"Manufacturing Equipment Knowledge","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Depending on the plant, students should understand the operating principles of equipment such as:"},{"type":"h","text":"Solid Dosage"},{"type":"h","text":"Rapid mixer granulator"},{"type":"h","text":"Fluid-bed dryer"},{"type":"h","text":"Blender"},{"type":"h","text":"Tablet compression machine"},{"type":"h","text":"Coating machine"},{"type":"h","text":"Capsule-filling machine"},{"type":"h","text":"Tablet deduster"},{"type":"h","text":"Metal detector"},{"type":"h","text":"Liquid Manufacturing"},{"type":"h","text":"Manufacturing vessels"},{"type":"h","text":"Mixing systems"},{"type":"h","text":"Homogenisers"},{"type":"h","text":"Filtration systems"},{"type":"h","text":"Filling machines"},{"type":"h","text":"Sterile Manufacturing"},{"type":"h","text":"Sterilisation systems"},{"type":"h","text":"Aseptic processing equipment"},{"type":"h","text":"Filling systems"},{"type":"h","text":"Cleanroom systems"},{"type":"h","text":"Packaging"},{"type":"h","text":"Blister packing machines"},{"type":"h","text":"Strip packing machines"},{"type":"h","text":"Bottle filling systems"},{"type":"h","text":"Labelling machines"},{"type":"h","text":"Cartoning systems"},{"type":"p","text":"The exact equipment depends on the manufacturing facility."}]},{"heading":"Documentation Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Pharmaceutical manufacturing is highly documentation-driven."},{"type":"p","text":"A Production Executive should be able to understand and accurately maintain:"},{"type":"h","text":"SOP"},{"type":"h","text":"│"},{"type":"h","text":"├── Process Instructions"},{"type":"h","text":"│"},{"type":"h","text":"├── Batch Manufacturing Record"},{"type":"h","text":"│"},{"type":"h","text":"├── Equipment Log"},{"type":"h","text":"│"},{"type":"h","text":"├── In-Process Checks"},{"type":"h","text":"│"},{"type":"h","text":"├── Yield Reconciliation"},{"type":"h","text":"│"},{"type":"h","text":"├── Deviation Record"},{"type":"h","text":"│"},{"type":"h","text":"└── CAPA / Change Control"},{"type":"h","text":"Critical Principle"},{"type":"p","text":"If an activity was not properly documented according to the approved system, it can be difficult to demonstrate that the activity was performed correctly."}]},{"heading":"Quality Control vs Production vs Quality Assurance","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understanding these differences is essential."},{"type":"table","header":["Function","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Production"},{"text":"Manufacture the product according to approved process"}],[{"text":"QC"},{"text":"Test materials, in-process samples and finished products"}],[{"text":"QA"},{"text":"Quality systems, compliance, review and oversight"}],[{"text":"Engineering"},{"text":"Equipment, utilities and technical systems"}],[{"text":"Warehouse"},{"text":"Materials and inventory"}],[{"text":"Regulatory"},{"text":"Regulatory submissions and compliance"}],[{"text":"Production Planning"},{"text":"Scheduling and capacity"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"A Production Executive must collaborate effectively with all these functions."}]},{"heading":"Problem-Solving Workflow","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"When a production problem occurs:"},{"type":"h","text":"Problem Detected"},{"type":"h","text":